# Default-deny: Dockerfile.cloudrun only needs app_v2.py, src/, config/, requirements.txt.
# Everything else (real clinic data, local credentials, backups, scratch scripts, docs,
# tests) is excluded by default so a future accidental file in the build context can never
# silently end up inside the image. New code must be added to app_v2.py/src/ to be shipped.
*

!app_v2.py
!requirements.txt
!src
!src/**
!config
!config/**

# Re-exclude anything secret-shaped even if it ends up under src/ or config/ later.
.env
.env.*
.supabase-runtime.env.local
config/email_research.env.local
config/gmail_oauth_client.json
config/gmail_oauth_token.json
config/outreach_email_v2.json
**/*.secret
**/*secrets*
**/.secrets/**
**/*.sqlite3*
**/*.db*
**/*.bak
**/*.csv
**/*.pem
**/*.key

# Build/runtime noise that must never ride along even under the allowed trees.
**/__pycache__/**
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache/**
**/.DS_Store
